.TH LPSD 8 2026-10-18 "Peios authd 0.0.24"
.SH NAME
lpsd \- Peios local principal source daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/sbin/lpsd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lpsd
owns the local principal database, verifies local credentials, and registers
with the Peios authentication authority as a Principal Source Interface
provider.  It cannot mint or install tokens.
.PP
The daemon also serves the local administration protocol used by
.BR lps (1)
on
.IR /run/lpsd/admin.sock ,
and, on
.IR /run/lpsd/self.sock ,
lets any authenticated principal read its own account and set its own
display name.  Requests there never name a principal: the subject is the
caller.  That socket is served without blocking, with at most 32 connections,
4 from any one user, 4 KiB a request and 5 seconds a connection.
It reports ready only after its source registration has been acknowledged by
.BR authd (8).
.PP
The service is normally started by peinit from the registry definition shipped
in
.IR /usr/share/regim/lpsd-service.reg .
It takes no command-line options.
.SH CREDENTIALS
Each principal has an explicit policy, a password verifier when present, and
up to 32 SSH public keys. SSH signatures are verified here against the exact
username and initial session hash bound by the trusted SSH monitor through PGSS.
Key probes do not authenticate. Revocation or policy changes invalidate pending
proofs; existing sessions are not terminated.
.PP
A principal may add or remove its own keys through
.BR authd (8)'s
logon socket.  lpsd asks for the current password first, so an account
with no password to prove (key-only, no credential, or no password set) is
refused and must ask an administrator.  Adding a key does not change the
credential policy.
.PP
This version reads store formats 4 and 5 and writes format 5.
Format 4 gains empty group descriptions and is rewritten on the next change.
Unsupported formats and corrupt stores are refused.
Do not delete an unreadable store to repair startup; preserve it for recovery.
A replacement store creates different identities.
.PP
The lpsd virtual service account owns the store.
Its protected descriptor grants access to that account and SYSTEM;
Administrators receive no direct grant.
.PP
A failed save does not always prove that the on-disk store is unchanged.
If synchronizing the directory fails after replacement, changed data can
be present with uncertain crash durability.
Stop administrative changes and investigate the storage failure.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/state/lpsd
Persistent local-principal state.
.TP
.I /run/lpsd/admin.sock
Local administration socket.
.TP
.I /run/lpsd/self.sock
A principal's own account: read it, and set its display name.  SYSTEM and
Administrators have full access; every authenticated principal may connect.
.TP
.I /run/psi.sock
Authentication-authority source socket.
.TP
.I /usr/share/regim/lpsd-authd-registration.reg
Seed which registers lpsd with the authority.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR authd (8),
.BR lps (1),
.BR login (1)
